cat > /workspace/epic_breakdown.txt << 'EOF'
================================================================================
EPIC BREAKDOWN: Self-Service Report Export Initiative
================================================================================
Epic ID: EPIC-EXPORT-001
Initiative: Self-Service Report Export for End Users and Administrators
Goal: Enable users to export filtered reports to PDF and CSV formats

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OVERVIEW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This epic delivers a self-service report export capability allowing end users 
and administrators to export their filtered reports to PDF and CSV formats. 
The feature includes audit logging for administrative oversight.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PERSONAS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. END USER
   - Primary consumer of report export functionality
   - Needs to export reports in PDF and CSV formats
   - Requires basic filtering capabilities

2. ADMINISTRATOR
   - Oversees export activity and compliance
   - Needs audit trail of all export operations
   - Requires ability to view export logs and statistics

3. POWER USER
   - Advanced filtering and date range capabilities
   - Frequent exporter of complex reports

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EPIC USER STORIES WITH ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STORY E-1: As an End User, I want to export a report to PDF so that I can 
           share it with stakeholders in a formatted document.

  Given I am logged in as an End User
  When I view a report and click the "Export to PDF" button
  Then the report is generated as a PDF file
  And the file downloads to my default download location
  And the filename includes the report name and timestamp

STORY E-2: As an End User, I want to export a report to CSV so that I can 
           analyze the data in spreadsheet applications.

  Given I am logged in as an End User
  When I view a report and click the "Export to CSV" button
  Then the report data is exported as a CSV file
  And the file downloads to my default download location
  And column headers are included in the first row

STORY E-3: As a Power User, I want to apply filters before exporting so that 
           I can export only the data relevant to my analysis.

  Given I am logged in as a Power User
  When I apply filters (date range, status, category) to a report
  And I click "Export" with my selected format
  Then the exported file contains only the filtered data
  And the filter criteria is noted in the export metadata

STORY E-4: As an Administrator, I want to view an audit log of all export 
           activities so that I can monitor compliance and usage.

  Given I am logged in as an Administrator
  When I navigate to the Export Audit page
  Then I see a list of all export activities
  And each entry shows: user, report name, format, timestamp, and file size
  And I can filter the audit log by user, date range, or format

STORY E-5: As an Administrator, I want to receive notifications for 
           bulk exports so that I can monitor unusual activity.

  Given I am logged in as an Administrator
  When a user exports more than 100 records in a single operation
  Then a notification is logged in the audit trail
  And the notification is flagged as "Bulk Export"

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EPIC ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA (Overall)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[ ] All user stories pass their Given-When-Then acceptance criteria
[ ] PDF exports render correctly with proper formatting
[ ] CSV exports are valid and importable in Excel/Google Sheets
[ ] Audit logging captures 100% of export activities
[ ] Performance: Export of 1000 records completes in under 30 seconds
[ ] Security: Users can only export reports they have permission to view
[ ] Accessibility: Export buttons are keyboard accessible and screen-reader friendly

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEPENDENCIES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Report viewing infrastructure (existing)
- User authentication/authorization system (existing)
- PDF generation library (new dependency)
- Audit logging system (existing - needs extension)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ESTIMATED EPIC SIZE: 42 points
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EOF

